# oracle: pair dpd/tstat alone, cut down from examples/PACKAGES/dpd-basic/dpd_tstat/in.dpd_tstat (cg SPC/E water), pair temperature 0 (no random force; the table of the example is a core pair and is left out)
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max relative error 4.4e-15 (thermo), 5.6e-16 (per-atom). Noise off (pair temperature 0). The example's table pair (hybrid/overlay table) is left out: measured alone, the core table pair differs from native by about 1e-7 per atom, so it is not part of this case.
# oracle-inputs: w77dpd_cg_spce.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=0
units            real
boundary     p p p
atom_style   atomic
dimension    3
newton       on
comm_modify  vel yes
read_data    w77dpd_cg_spce.data
pair_style       dpd/tstat 0.0 0.0 10.0 385262
pair_coeff   1 1 10.0 10.0
timestep    1.0
run_style   verlet
velocity all create 300.0 68768932
thermo_style custom step time temp press pe ke
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo       5
fix 1 all    nve
run          20
